<section class="hero">
  <h1>A commons for the civilization of the Dao</h1>
  <p>We do not ask which classic a teaching comes from, which master or lineage stands behind it, or which religion you belong to. If you can express the wisdom of the Dao in today's language, and you accept two baselines — <strong>human rights</strong> and <strong>coexistence</strong> — you have a place here.</p>
  <p class="hero-actions"><a class="btn" href="/en/charter/">Read the Charter</a> <a class="btn ghost" href="/zh/library/">Browse the library (Chinese)</a></p>
</section>
<div class="columns two">
  <section class="col"><h2>Keep</h2><p>A public, durable, downloadable archive for contemporary thought on the Dao — including new work from mainland China that has no safe home there.</p></section>
  <section class="col"><h2>Show</h2><p>Every community or individual ("dojo") gets an equal, self-managed page. No lineage required.</p></section>
  <section class="col"><h2>Connect</h2><p>Dialogue across traditions — Daoist, Buddhist, other faiths, philosophy and the sciences.</p></section>
</div>
<p>Most content is in Chinese. English articles will appear as contributors publish them.</p>
